# newdoc id = texts/birchbark/363
# date_created = 1380-1400
# transl_ru = Поклон от Семена невестке моей. Если ты еще не поминала, то [имей в виду:] у тебя солод был. Солод ржаной в подклете. Ты возьми пригоршню (?), а муки сколько нужно, и испеки [пирога] в меру. А мясо на сеннике. А что [касается того, чтобы] дать рубль Игнату, то ты дай.
# transl_en_1 = Greetings from Semen to my bride. If, perhaps, you do not remember, then [consider this]: you had the malt. The malt is made of rye [and is kept] in the storage space. Take a handful (?) [of the malt] and however much of the flour and bake [a pie] to a measure (i.e., enough). And the meat is in the sennik (i.e., a cold storage space outside of a hayloft). And [in regard to] giving the ruble to Ignat, then give it to him.
# transl_en_2 = A bow from Smen to my daughter-in-law. In case you have not celebrated the commemoration meal: you had malt, and the rye malt is in the cellar. You take a handful, and as much flour as you need, and you bake it in the (proper) measure. And the meat is in the pantry. And concerning the rouble that is due to Ignat, you give it.
